# ============================================================================
# Line-ending policy -- deliberately NARROW.
#
# This file pins LF for the generated-ABI surface ONLY. It is not a repo-wide
# `* text=auto` policy: that would renormalize every tracked file on the next
# checkout, which is a much larger and riskier change than the problem below.
#
# Why these files. `make check-abi` compares the two ABI facades against the
# canonical constants in scripts/gen-user-abi.py (see CANONICAL_SHIM_* there):
# canonical UTF-8 text, modulo line endings. check_shim_form() normalizes
# newlines on read precisely so a core.autocrlf=true checkout -- which clang
# compiles identically -- does not fail the gate. Pinning LF here is the OTHER
# half of that: it keeps the repository side canonical so the normalization is
# a safety net for pre-existing clones rather than the thing the contract rests
# on. The two defenses are independent on purpose.
#
# The generated contract is listed for the same reason -- gen-user-abi.py
# renders it with LF and --check compares the rendering against the file.
# ============================================================================

abi/generated/abi_contract.h   text eol=lf
include/kernel/abi_hash.h      text eol=lf
user/include/abi_numbers.h     text eol=lf
scripts/gen-user-abi.py        text eol=lf
